schema: "0.4"
id: chat-ux-v2-room
type: image
quality: high

# Chat UX v2 redesigned room view (ticket d8a6e4ef).
# Consumes Yuki's v2 redesign flow + inspectable-identity refinement, Lena's
# reserved UI channel + sg- design tokens, and the console pattern's shared
# language (7e269bff). This is also Theo's hero-demo frame (persona peek).

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PREMIUM team-chat surface inside a developer console — calm, dense, modern,
    dark-themed (think Linear / Height, not a consumer messenger, not a game).
    Clean humanist sans-serif throughout (NO serif body). Restrained chrome,
    generous information density, excellent small-size legibility.

    IDENTITY IS THE HERO: this chat is between named AI PERSONAS, and their
    authored identity must be legible and inspectable — each speaker has a stable
    color-dot avatar + name + role, and one persona's "peek" popover is open
    showing their authored bio + an accruing journal. That inspectable identity is
    the whole point of the shot.

    COLOR DISCIPLINE: UI chrome is achromatic (graphite/slate surfaces, white/muted
    text). The only saturated color comes from (a) per-persona avatar dots drawn
    from a distinct, evenly-spaced hue set reserved for identity, and (b) reaction
    chips. Selection/focus uses a single reserved accent (cool teal/cyan), never a
    rainbow. Status/role chips use muted tints, never loud brand hues.
  text: |
    A 16:9 mockup of a redesigned team-chat room in a dark developer console.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands):
    - LEFT: a slim app nav rail (icons, achromatic) — secondary, just for context.
    - CENTER (dominant): the message THREAD, full readable width.
    - RIGHT (~280px): a collapsible INFO PANEL with a collapse chevron in the header.

    ROOM HEADER BAND (top of center+right):
    - Room name "work-group" in medium-weight sans.
    - A copyable MONO SLUG CHIP "#work-group" (subtle graphite pill, mono font).
    - Topic line (muted): "Standing open work group — coordination".
    - A small stacked MEMBER-AVATAR CLUSTER (4–5 overlapping color dots + "+6").
    - An info-panel toggle (chevron) at the right edge.

    THE THREAD (center) — sender-GROUPED, lighter rows, NOT boxed cards:
    - Messages grouped by sender into blocks. Each block: a COLOR-DOT AVATAR
      (a filled circle with the speaker's initial, each persona a distinct
      reserved hue) + persona NAME + a small muted ROLE CHIP (e.g. "UX",
      "Architect", "QA") + a muted right-aligned timestamp — rendered ONCE at the
      top of the run; the following 1–2 lines from the same persona are tight body
      text indented under the identity, no repeated avatar.
    - Show ~4 grouped blocks from different personas (distinct dot hues): e.g.
      "Yuki · UX", "Dmitri · Architect", "Sofia · QA", "Marcus · Backend".
    - A subtle DATE DIVIDER ("Today") separates an earlier run.
    - Rows are light: no heavy borders/card backgrounds; one row shows a faint
      hover background with a small right-aligned ACTION CLUSTER revealed
      (a react "+" and a kebab) — the affordance appears on hover, it is NOT an
      always-on dashed circle under every message.
    - Under two messages: compact REACTION COUNT CHIPS (e.g. "👍 3", "🎉 1"),
      one chip in a "mine" selected state (subtle teal fill + readable count).

    THE HERO MOMENT — a PERSONA PEEK popover, open over Yuki's avatar:
    - A small dark rounded popover anchored to the clicked avatar, showing:
      the color-dot + "Yuki Tanaka" + a "UX Designer" role chip; a 1–2 line BIO
      ("Research-led UX designer; thinks in journeys, states, and the quiet moments
       where users get confused"); a tiny "Journal" section with 2 recent entries
      (short timestamped lines, visibly accruing); a "Knowledge base · 8" count;
      and a muted "view persona →" link.
    - This popover is the focal point — it makes the persona's AUTHORED, inspectable
      identity literally readable. Give it a soft focus ring (reserved teal).

    RIGHT INFO PANEL:
    - "Topic" (room description) + the copyable mono slug chip.
    - "Present" — a vertical list of persona rows (color dot + name + role).
    - "Pinned" — 1–2 linked-artifact rows (doc icon + title), muted.

    COMPOSER (bottom of center): a clean single-row input width-aligned to the
    thread + a primary Send button; placeholder "Write a message…".

    MOOD: premium, dense, calm, dark. Sans-serif everywhere. Color only on persona
    dots + reaction chips + the one teal focus accent. This should look like a tool
    a team actually lives in — and the persona peek should make you believe these
    teammates have real, authored identities.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    identity_legibility: {weight: 3, description: "Sender-grouped blocks each with a color-dot avatar + name + role chip + muted timestamp rendered once per run; distinct reserved hues per persona; an OPEN persona-peek popover showing bio + accruing journal + KB count + view-persona link (the hero moment)"}
    density_and_rows: {weight: 3, description: "Light grouped rows (not boxed cards), tighter vertical rhythm, a date divider, hover-revealed action cluster on one row (NOT an always-on dashed + circle), compact reaction count chips with one 'mine' state"}
    color_discipline: {weight: 2, description: "Achromatic graphite chrome + sans-serif; saturated color only on persona dots + reaction chips; a single reserved teal focus/selection accent; muted role/status chips — no rainbow chrome, no serif body"}
    layout: {weight: 2, description: "Full-width thread + collapsible right info panel (topic/slug chip/present-personas/pinned); a real room header band with name + mono copyable slug chip + topic + member-avatar cluster; width-aligned composer"}
  reject_if:
    - "always-on dashed + reaction circle under every message (the v1 antipattern)"
    - "heavy boxed message cards with large whitespace / low density"
    - "serif body font or consumer-messenger/game aesthetic"
    - "rainbow UI chrome or no visible persona-peek popover"
    - "dead empty grey right column instead of a populated info panel"

tags: [chat, ux-v2, mockup, ui, persona-identity, npl-frontend, hero-demo]
